protocol.description:
An app publishes its menus (the app menu, File, Edit, View, Window, Help and its own)
and the menu bar shows them while the app is frontmost. The model is a JSON document
passed in a file descriptor, replaced as a whole on every change; the bar sends the
chosen item back to the app. Keyboard shortcuts stay with the app: the model only
describes them, the app handles the keys itself while it has the keyboard.

The model (UTF-8 JSON, at most max_model_size bytes):

  { "menus": [ menu, … ] }
  menu: { "label": string, "role": "app" | "window" | "help" | "" , "items": [ item, … ] }
  item: { "id": uint, "label": string, "enabled": bool, "checked": bool,
          "role": string, "shortcut": shortcut, "items": [ item, … ] }
        | { "separator": true }
  shortcut: { "key": string, "meta": bool, "ctrl": bool, "alt": bool, "shift": bool }

An item with "items" is a submenu. "id" is chosen by the app and comes back in
activated. An item with a "role" is provided by the system (quit, hide, minimize…):
the bar runs it itself and may give it its own label. Unknown keys are ignored.
